#   Classes
############################

# Class: pmd:PMD_3ebdc587_15fa_41a1_922f_3d46f0748afe (specification document)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label pmd:PMD_3ebdc587_15fa_41a1_922f_3d46f0748afe "specification document"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition pmd:PMD_3ebdc587_15fa_41a1_922f_3d46f0748afe "A document intended to communicate one or more directive information entities or descriptive specifications"@en)
SubClassOf(pmd:PMD_3ebdc587_15fa_41a1_922f_3d46f0748afe obo:IAO_0000310)
SubClassOf(pmd:PMD_3ebdc587_15fa_41a1_922f_3d46f0748afe ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 ObjectUnionOf(obo:IAO_0000033 pmd:PMD_44f238dd_bef8_4582_a2c4_3915b1d5496b)))

# Class: pmd:PMD_44f238dd_bef8_4582_a2c4_3915b1d5496b (descriptive specification)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000116 pmd:PMD_44f238dd_bef8_4582_a2c4_3915b1d5496b "Descriptive specification is introduced for non-directive reference content that establishes descriptions, meanings, designations, or classifications. Its intended function differs from that of a data item, which records or represents data; a textual entity, which concerns textual form; an identifier, which identifies something; a value specification, which specifies a quantitative or categorical value; and a directive information entity, whose concretizations indicate to their bearer how to realize them in a process. These distinctions are functional; no formal disjointness is asserted"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment pmd:PMD_44f238dd_bef8_4582_a2c4_3915b1d5496b "A descriptive specification represents how subject matter is characterized, defined, designated, or classified, rather than prescribing an action or intended outcome. Examples include terminology definitions, classification schemes, and material designations."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label pmd:PMD_44f238dd_bef8_4582_a2c4_3915b1d5496b "descriptive specification"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition pmd:PMD_44f238dd_bef8_4582_a2c4_3915b1d5496b "An information content entity whose concretizations describe characteristics, structure, meaning, designation, or classification of some subject matter."@en)
SubClassOf(pmd:PMD_44f238dd_bef8_4582_a2c4_3915b1d5496b obo:IAO_0000030)

# Class: pmd:PMD_a584461c_2ab4_4861_804a_2f77661bba08 (standard)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000116 pmd:PMD_a584461c_2ab4_4861_804a_2f77661bba08 "In materials science and engineering, processes, measurements, artifacts, and datasets frequently refer to formal or internal standards. Decision was to place the standard class under 'specification document', rather than 'directive information entity', as standards may contain non-directive terminology, classifications, designations, or data-format conventions. The hierarchy remains shallow, leaving specific standard types to application ontologies and particular standards, issuing bodies, and their relations to ABox modelling"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment pmd:PMD_a584461c_2ab4_4861_804a_2f77661bba08 "A standard may specify requirements, guidelines, or accepted practices to which processes, artifacts, procedures, or datasets are expected to conform. It may also define controlled terminology, classifications, material designations, or data formats. Some standards are themselves directive information entities or have directive information entities, such as plan specifications, as parts; others primarily define terminology or conventions"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label pmd:PMD_a584461c_2ab4_4861_804a_2f77661bba08 "standard"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:altLabel pmd:PMD_a584461c_2ab4_4861_804a_2f77661bba08 "Norm"@de)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition pmd:PMD_a584461c_2ab4_4861_804a_2f77661bba08 "A specification document that is issued or maintained by a standardization body and provides rules, requirements, guidelines, characteristics, practices, or terminology intended for wide adoption and common or repeated use within a specified context"@en)
SubClassOf(pmd:PMD_a584461c_2ab4_4861_804a_2f77661bba08 pmd:PMD_3ebdc587_15fa_41a1_922f_3d46f0748afe)


